mlmf-onnx - third-party provenance notice

mlmf-onnx itself is licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. The wire layout it writes is
read from onnx/onnx's `onnx.proto` (Apache-2.0); the details, revision and
licence text are in the repository's top-level NOTICE and in
LICENSE-onnx-Apache-2.0.txt beside this file.


The field numbers, wire types and message nesting that `crates/mlmf-onnx`
writes (`ModelProto`, `GraphProto`, `TensorProto`, `ValueInfoProto`,
`TypeProto`, `OperatorSetIdProto`, `StringStringEntryProto`, and the
`TensorProto.DataType` codes) are read from `onnx/onnx.proto` in `onnx/onnx`
at tag `v1.23.2` (commit `e1ac8e74b620bbdc7ba07f0440806bd93f651a28`; the file's
blob is `4118be57634cf400875dc476d00c7140c5f96262`). The file declares
`SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0`, and the repository's `LICENSE` is
Apache 2.0 (GitHub licence API, checked 2026-10-25); the licence text as the
tag serves it, sha256
`cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30`, is
`crates/mlmf-onnx/LICENSE-onnx-Apache-2.0.txt`. No source from `onnx` is
copied: they are facts about a file format, and the writer is original code.

`crates/mlmf-onnx/tests/golden.onnx` is output of the `onnx` Python package
(1.23.2, with protobuf 7.36.2), generated by `crates/mlmf-onnx/tests/
make_golden.py` (`pip install onnx==1.23.2`, then `python make_golden.py
golden.onnx`). It is a 240-byte model of invented values, kept so the writer
can be compared byte for byte against another implementation.

`crates/mlmf-onnx/tests/conv1d.onnx` is `onnx/backend/test/data/
pytorch-converted/test_Conv1d/model.onnx` as the `onnx` 1.23.2 wheel ships it
(525 bytes, sha256
`6784029f6f72d5d8c9dc9667b858f838882c02aa92663e3b8c9f85a50a9cf10e`),
unmodified: a model PyTorch's own exporter wrote, kept so the reader is
checked against a file this project did not produce. It is part of the `onnx`
repository and so under the same Apache-2.0 licence (text:
`crates/mlmf-onnx/LICENSE-onnx-Apache-2.0.txt`). `crates/mlmf-onnx/tests/
variants.onnx` is generated from invented values by `make_read_fixtures.py`
beside it, which also writes the `read-*.tsv` files from the reference
package's reading of the three models.
